---
import Notebooks from '../../components/Notebooks';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO_URL } from '../../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Notebooks"
  description="The analysis notebooks, executed against the current data build after every export."
>
  <section>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Notebooks</h1>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
      Five analyses that run on every published build: whether the Streamers sorts pick the right players, what game context, shooting streaks and a
      teammate's absence are worth, and how far the data can be trusted, re-asked of the newest data. Each opens as a rendered page; the source lives in the
      repository under <code>notebooks/</code> and runs locally, against the published build, or against the lakehouse.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">
      The board itself is judged by the walk-forward backtest, on the lakehouse rebuilt as it stood on past days (<a
        href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/docs/adr/0018-point-in-time-builds.md`}
        class="underline underline-offset-4"
        rel="noopener">ADR 0018</a
      >). The <a href="/methodology/" class="underline underline-offset-4">Methodology</a> page gives the evidence for each of its numbers.
    </p>
    <!-- a screen tall while the island loads, so the footer starts below the fold and nothing shifts (#436) -->
    <div class="mt-6 min-h-screen">
      <Notebooks client:only="react" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
